{"artifacts":[],"cancelled_at":null,"effects":[],"expected_sha":"1b2f4854913f105446b63c747b6de491c0be62f9","generation":1,"intent":{"claim":"7440475f9924460a8f59784de724c257","dispatch_status":"acknowledged","id":"0cc4ae3df9e244b1a66a617dd34a5e48","recorded_at":1791299378},"iteration":1,"next_check_at":1791299678,"phase":"d679346797ae4c40a47670998b516bea","publications":[],"reason":null,"report":null,"request":{"authorized_actor_id":218610,"baseline_review_ids":[5394813030,5397926347,5398173650,5398273007,5398651625,5401825565,5401972896,5402105477,5402254937,5402389957,5402509972,5402610899,5402716853,5402833170,5403071260,5403267202,5403439730,5403510542,5403571266],"budgets":{"deadline_seconds":7200,"max_iterations":5,"propagation_seconds":120,"retention_days":14,"worker_timeout_minutes":30},"commit_author":{"id":218610,"login":"trask"},"deadline":1791306576,"findings":[{"body":"<!-- ccr-overview-v2 -->\n\n## Copilot review overview\n\n### \ud83d\udd35 Needs a closer look\n\nCross-run delivery matching and race-sensitive production force-cancellation warrant human sign-off.\n\n**Review effort:** Balanced  \n**Findings:** 1 <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/high-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/high-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/high-v2-light.png\" alt=\"High severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> \u00b7 1 <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Medium severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture>\n\n<details open>\n<summary><strong>Open (2)</strong></summary>\n\n- <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/high-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/high-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/high-v2-light.png\" alt=\"High severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> [Coverage search misses replacements split across run slices](#discussion_r4175448985)\n- <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Medium severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> [Cross-PR publisher recovery is blocked by scope check](#discussion_r4171051071)\n</details>","comment_id":null,"key":"review:5403571266","kind":"body","line":null,"path":null,"review_id":5403571266},{"body":"If PR 1's publisher is stalled and PR 2's publisher is waiting for the same repository, this scope check rejects the replacement. The test at `test_workflow_watchdog.mjs:1947\u20131956` explicitly expects no cancellation, so the cross-PR recovery promised in the description and setup guide remains unsupported. Removing this guard alone is unsafe: targeted delivery passes `--pr-number` and does not cover the other PR. Add a recovery path that preserves the older PR's delivery, or narrow the description and guide to same-PR or repository-wide replacements.","comment_commit_id":"1b2f4854913f105446b63c747b6de491c0be62f9","comment_id":4171051071,"key":"inline:4171051071","kind":"inline","line":442,"original_commit_id":"e49acfb56f7e4071f223ccd4c364891f660ea0fa","original_line":349,"path":".github/scripts/pull-request-dashboard/netlify/lib/workflow-watchdog.mjs","review_commit_id":"e49acfb56f7e4071f223ccd4c364891f660ea0fa","review_id":5398273007,"review_submitted_at":"2026-10-03T01:10:00Z","root_author":{"id":175728472,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA","type":"Bot"},"thread_context":[{"author":{"id":175728472,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA","type":"Bot"},"body_hash":"2b52c13dccaecb15d95558e88806cbe2975793a85754c087617d286f72aae1b5","id":4171051071,"parent":null,"updated_at":"2026-10-03T01:10:00Z"}],"thread_id":"PRRT_kwDOTENyc86oiZEe"},{"body":"These slices can keep a recoverable multi-repository backfill stalled indefinitely. With one stale scheduled run, eight newer unrelated manual runs, and fourteen older manual candidates, the seven-slot rotation alternates between two disjoint halves. If repo-a's only covering publisher is in one half and repo-b's is in the other, they are never fetched together. `jobsByRun` is rebuilt each invocation, so `findPublisherReplacements` always rejects the incomplete coverage. Retain discovered covering runs across slices and revalidate them together before cancellation, or use a lookup strategy that can assemble coverage for every unfinished publisher. Add a regression with the required replacements in different slices.","comment_commit_id":"1b2f4854913f105446b63c747b6de491c0be62f9","comment_id":4175448985,"key":"inline:4175448985","kind":"inline","line":143,"original_commit_id":"66cf58bd4fb37d0d42eea6be52af3f791d5d9d41","original_line":127,"path":".github/scripts/pull-request-dashboard/netlify/lib/workflow-watchdog.mjs","review_commit_id":"66cf58bd4fb37d0d42eea6be52af3f791d5d9d41","review_id":5403510542,"review_submitted_at":"2026-10-03T23:52:32Z","root_auth